    {
      "title": "Externalized Config and the 12-Factor Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Externalized Config and the 12-Factor Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What Counts as Config",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Config = anything that ==varies between deploys==",
                "Examples: **DB URL**, credentials, hostnames, API keys",
                "Code does not vary, so keep the two ==separate=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. 12-Factor Rule III",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Build once",
                    "sub": "one artifact",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Dev",
                    "sub": "env config",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Staging",
                    "sub": "env config",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Prod",
                    "sub": "env config",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Store config in the ==environment==, never in the codebase",
                "Artifact is promoted ==unchanged== through every stage"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "application-prod.yml",
                "Env vars"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Grows with",
                  "every new environment",
                  "nothing: {green:orthogonal}"
                ],
                [
                  "Grouped by",
                  "environment name",
                  "{green:never}"
                ],
                [
                  "Lives in",
                  "the repo",
                  "the deploy"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Prove the Separation",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Litmus test:** could you ==open-source the repo now== without leaking a credential?",
                "If not, config is leaking into code",
                "**Prove it:** litmus test plus a secret scan of the repo",
                "**Why one build?** The tested artifact is what ships"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "git grep -iE \"password|secret|api_key\""
              ],
              "note": "any hit with a real value means a leak"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "One artifact, many deploys",
              "text": "Per-environment files as the **main** mechanism multiply with every new environment."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Env Vars, Config Servers and Precedence",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Env Vars, Config Servers and Precedence",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Env Vars vs Config Servers",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Env vars",
                "Config server"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Plus",
                  "Simple, any language, everywhere",
                  "Central, versioned, per-app/profile"
                ],
                [
                  "Minus",
                  "Flat strings, no audit, in `/proc`",
                  "Needs a server"
                ],
                [
                  "Update",
                  "Restart needed",
                  "Dynamic refresh"
                ],
                [
                  "Tools",
                  "Any runtime",
                  "Spring Cloud Config, Consul KV, etcd, AppConfig, SSM"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Precedence and Binding",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "CLI flags",
                    "sub": "wins",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Env vars",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Config server",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "File",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Defaults",
                    "sub": "loses",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Know your framework's order==",
                "Rule of thumb: ==closest to the process wins==",
                "Spring Boot: remote properties rank below env vars and CLI args",
                "Env var names map to property keys (==relaxed binding==)"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "export SPRING_DATASOURCE_URL=jdbc:postgresql://db/app"
              ],
              "note": "binds to spring.datasource.url"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Startup Checks and Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Fail fast== on a missing required key",
                "Validate types when binding"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Logging full config or env, or crash dumps, leaks secrets",
                "Hard server dependency: cache ==last-known-good== config, set sane defaults"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "text": "**Env vs server?** Env is simple but needs a restart; a server is central and refreshes live. **No redeploy?** Server refresh. **Order?** CLI > env > server > file > defaults."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Kubernetes ConfigMaps and Secrets",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Kubernetes ConfigMaps and Secrets",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. ConfigMap and Secret",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:ConfigMap}: non-sensitive key/values or whole files",
                "{red:Secret}: sensitive data, same shape, values ==base64== in `data`",
                "base64 is **encoding, not encryption**"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "kubectl create configmap app-cfg --from-literal=LOG_LEVEL=info --from-file=app.properties",
                "kubectl create secret generic db --from-literal=password=s3cret"
              ],
              "note": "create both from the CLI"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Consuming and Updates",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Way",
                "How",
                "Updates"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "env",
                  "`valueFrom.configMapKeyRef` / `secretKeyRef`",
                  "{red:fixed at start}"
                ],
                [
                  "envFrom",
                  "imports all keys",
                  "{red:fixed at start}"
                ],
                [
                  "volume",
                  "each key becomes a file",
                  "{green:refreshes eventually}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Volume refresh waits on the kubelet sync; ==subPath== mounts never refresh",
                "Env change needs `kubectl rollout restart deploy/app`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Secure and Freeze",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Harden Secrets",
              "items": [
                "Enable ==etcd encryption== at rest",
                "Restrict RBAC `get` access",
                "Prefer External Secrets, Vault, CSI Secrets Store"
              ],
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`immutable: true` blocks edits and cuts API server watch load",
                "Roll out a **new name**; hash the name in Helm/Kustomize to trigger a restart"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Secret is ==not encrypted== by default. Env vars need a restart; volumes refresh."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Feature Flags: Release vs Ops",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Feature Flags: Release vs Ops",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Flag Types",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Feature flag== = runtime conditional: code ships dark, a toggle releases it",
                "Decouples **deploy** from **release**, no redeploy"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Type",
                "Lifetime",
                "Use"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Release",
                  "short",
                  "hides unfinished work"
                ],
                [
                  "Experiment",
                  "short",
                  "A/B test"
                ],
                [
                  "Ops",
                  "long",
                  "kill switch"
                ],
                [
                  "Permission",
                  "very long",
                  "entitlements"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Release vs Ops",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:Release} flags: delete at 100% rollout",
                "{red:Ops} flags: permanent, on-call sheds load or disables a failing dependency",
                "Target by user ID, segment or percentage",
                "Hash user ID + flag key: ==sticky variant=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "js",
              "lines": [
                "if (flags.isEnabled('new-checkout', user)) {",
                "  newCheckout()",
                "} else { oldCheckout() }"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Evaluation",
              "items": [
                "Server SDK: cached rules, in-memory check",
                "Client-side exposes rules: no secrets"
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Safe default",
              "text": "Flag service unreachable? Fall back to the old path."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Deploy vs release?** Deploy ships code; release exposes it.",
                "**Lifetimes?** Release: short; kill switch: permanent.",
                "**Sticky variant?** Hash stable user ID + flag key."
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Dark Launches, Progressive Rollout and Flag Debt",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Dark Launches, Progressive Rollout and Flag Debt",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Dark Launch",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Dark launch==: new path runs in prod on real traffic, ==no user-visible effect==",
                "Shadow traffic or mirrored reads: compare responses, discard result",
                "{red:Never mirror writes} with side effects"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Progressive Rollout",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Staff",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "1%",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "5%",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "25%",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "50%",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "100%",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Watch ==error rate== and ==latency== at each step",
                "Roll back by ==flipping the flag==, not redeploying"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Dark vs Canary vs Blue/Green",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Dark launch",
                "Canary",
                "Blue/green"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Idea",
                  "Hidden from users",
                  "Small slice of real users",
                  "Swap whole environments"
                ],
                [
                  "Level",
                  "**Feature**",
                  "Deploy",
                  "Deploy"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Flag Debt and Cleanup",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Stale flags: dead branches, ==2^N untested combinations==, surprise behavior",
                "Every flag gets an ==owner==, a ==type== and an ==expiry date==",
                "Open the ==removal ticket== when the flag is created",
                "At 100% for a settled period: delete flag and losing path in ==one change==",
                "CI or lint check fails on flags past expiry",
                "Keep a ==flag inventory=="
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Flags are ==temporary== unless ops or permission: no expiry means debt."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
